{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And one who strikes an animal shall pay for it.</b> Above He spoke of one who kills an animal, and here He speaks of one who wounds it." "<b>And one who strikes a person shall be put to death.</b> Even if he did not kill him but only made a wound in him — for נפשׁ is not said here. And Scripture spoke of one who strikes his father and his mother, and it comes to liken him to one who strikes an animal: just as one who strikes an animal is from among the living, so too one who strikes his father is from among the living — excluding one who strikes after death. For we find that one who curses after death is liable; it was necessary to say that one who strikes is exempt. And just as with an animal it is by injury — for if there is no injury there are no restitution payments — so too one who strikes his father is not liable until he makes a wound in him (Sifra; Sanhedrin 4)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:13.346550899Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}